# London Bridge (repertoire plan: london-bridge). The traditional English nursery song with its
# first verse, in G in first position, 8 bars of 2/4, played twice. "Lon-don" is a dotted eighth
# and a sixteenth: long-short.
# Notes: G = open string 3, A = string 3 fret 2 (finger 2), B = open string 2, C = string 2
# fret 1 (finger 1), D = string 2 fret 3 (finger 3), E = open string 1. The teacher plays one
# chord per bar: G G | D7 G | G G | D7 G. From level 3, once D7 is learned, swap parts.
title: London Bridge
id: london-bridge
composer: Traditional English
source: Nursery song; the rhyme in print in the 18th century; arranged for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (traditional); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 2
tags: melody, lyrics, nursery rhyme, 2/4, dotted rhythm
tempo: 92
time: 2/4
key: G

